-"""
-Design analysis for the D13 variant.
-
-variant_spec:
-  concretization:
-    legend:
-      shape: an isolated 2x2 block on exactly one grid edge, never in a corner
-      reading:
-        top:    outer row = host colors, inner row = fill colors
-        bottom: outer row = host colors, inner row = fill colors
-        left:   outer col = host colors, inner col = fill colors
-        right:  outer col = host colors, inner col = fill colors
-      semantics: two aligned color pairs encode A->X and B->Y
-      visibility: the block is surrounded by a 1-cell black halo inside the grid, so it reads as a deliberate key rather than region noise
-    regions:
-      kept_from_source: two large noisy foreground regions on black background, plus black dents
-    dents:
-      kept_from_source: detect dents after cleaning 1-cell specks/protrusions
-      changed_step: patch color comes from legend mapping instead of hard-coded opposite-color swap
-
-  behavior_trace:
-    original:
-      a dent in color A always stamps color B, and a dent in color B always stamps color A
-    variant_example:
-      if the legend says A->third and B->A, then:
-      - a dent inside region A becomes a 3x3 third-color patch with teal center
-      - a dent inside region B becomes a 3x3 A-color patch with teal center
-    difference:
-      host-color detection is unchanged; only the host->patch lookup source changes
-
-  complexity_calibration:
-    mapping_choices:
-      allowed in generated data: {other color, third color}
-      guarantee: at least one host maps to the third color, so samples do not collapse back to the original binary swap
-    support:
-      each sample contains dents in both regions, so both legend pairs are exercised repeatedly
-
-  implicit_assumption_audit:
-    old_assumption:
-      _clean_foreground can treat every non-main color as disposable noise
-    fix:
-      legend cells are masked out before cleaning, dent detection, and main-color counting
-    old_assumption:
-      patch color is derivable from the other main color alone
-    fix:
-      patch color must be looked up from the decoded legend using the host color as the key
-
-  placement_legality:
-    generator_constraints:
-      - legend is placed only in an all-black 2x2 edge pocket with a 1-cell interior halo
-      - bg noise is forbidden inside the legend halo
-      - dents still obey the original spacing and host-majority constraints
-    solver_alignment:
-      the same halo rule is used by the solver to recover the legend reliably
-
-  observability_and_cleanliness:
-    why_humans_can_infer_it:
-      - the legend is a small isolated symbol on the border, visually separate from the main scene
-      - one mapping uses a third color in every generated sample, making the legend materially necessary
-      - dents remain abundant, so the same legend-driven color choice repeats many times
-    avoided_failure_mode:
-      identity mappings are not generated, because they would hide the 3x3 patch and make the new rule harder to see
-"""
+# Design analysis
+# - Concrete appearance:
+#   The original scene stays intact: two large foreground regions sit on black,
+#   black dents are punched into them, and a few single-cell noise pixels are
+#   scattered in background or on the region boundary. The D13 change adds one
+#   isolated 2x2 legend block on a grid edge. The outer edge row/column lists
+#   the two host colors; the adjacent inner row/column lists the colors to use
+#   for that host's dent patch. Because there are only two hosts, a fixed 2x2
+#   legend is enough and keeps the symbolic step visually obvious.
+# - Behavior trace:
+#   Original logic: if a dent belongs to region A, stamp color B; if it belongs
+#   to region B, stamp color A. New logic: read the legend first. Example:
